# Atlas Backend Rules

- Use modular monolith boundaries.
- API handlers validate inputs and delegate to services.
- Domain services own business rules.
- Eve tools in `apps/agent` call Atlas domain/application services only; no second memory store.
- Repositories centralize DB access.
- External providers go through ports/adapters.
- Fake/local provider adapters must exist for ordinary local development unless explicitly deferred by an issue.
- Long-running Workflow SDK jobs must be idempotent.
- Writes must be attributable to user, AI, system, or integration.
- External actions must use P1 risk levels (auto drafts/internal; confirm real external writes).
- Do not leak raw provider errors to users.
